## Capabilities

Each selected capability is one module under `src/capabilities/`, one section under `config/`,
one provider the kernel boots, and one or two routes that exercise it against the real backend.
A backend that does not answer at Boot **fails Boot** and rolls back what booted before it; a
substitute never stands in.

{% if cap_cache %}
{% if example_domain %}
- **cache** — Valkey; `GET /cache/ping` round-trips; `GET /items/{id}` is read through the cache and every write invalidates.
{% else %}
- **cache** — Valkey; `GET /cache/ping` round-trips; the cache is published for your handlers.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% if cap_jobs %}
- **jobs** — a worker on the `default` queue with the `starter.echo` handler; `POST /jobs` enqueues (`{"key","message"}`), `GET /jobs/{id}` reads the state. The store is this application's own database row.
{% endif %}
{% if cap_mail %}
- **mail** — SMTP; the relay is verified at Boot; `POST /mail/notice` sends one message (`{"to","subject"}`){% if auth_session %}, and the authentication flows send their verification and reset mail through it{% endif %}.
{% endif %}
{% if cap_storage %}
- **storage** — objects under `var/objects` (git-ignored, created before Boot); `PUT /files/{name}` stores the body, `GET /files/{name}` reads it back.
{% endif %}
